Day 9 – Bubble Sort (Understanding the Algorithm)

Today I started learning Bubble Sort.

Instead of writing the code immediately, I first focused on understanding how the algorithm works. I traced each comparison and swap by hand. This made it much easier to understand why the largest element moves to the end after every pass.

What I Learned

* Bubble Sort compares only neighboring elements.
* If the left element is greater than the right element, they are swapped.
* After every pass, the largest unsorted element reaches its correct position at the end.
* If an array is already sorted, we can stop early by checking whether any swap happened during a pass.

